    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 50 tests pass \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI made the `householdId` deterministic and reworked household duplicate detection accordingly.\n\n**`AssignHouseholdId.java`** \u2014 now computes the id for *every* owner as the first 12 hex chars of `SHA-256(normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode)` (lastName normalized case-insensitively / whitespace-collapsed via `RequireUniqueOwnerHousehold.normalize`). No longer conditional on `sharesHousehold`, and the old back-fill loop is gone \u2014 since the value is derived purely from `(lastName, postcode)`, existing members already carry the same id.\n\n**`RequireUniqueOwnerHousehold.java`** \u2014 rekeyed from `(lastName, address)` to the computed `householdId`: rejects 409 when an existing owner shares it, bypassed by `sharesHousehold`. It now takes `@Val Owner` (for the computed id) alongside the request.\n\n**`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the previously-inert `RequireUniqueOwnerHousehold` back into the pipeline as `requireHousehold`, between `assignHousehold` (which populates the id) and `identity` (the identity-key check). So `sharesHousehold` bypasses the household block but a same-telephone member still collides on the identity key.\n\n**`AssignPossibleDuplicate.java`** \u2014 a declared household member (`sharesHousehold` true) is no longer flagged: `possibleDuplicate=false`, `possibleDuplicateOf` cleared. Any non-declared same-`(lastName, postcode)` owner is already blocked upstream with 409.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `householdId`, `sharesHousehold`, `identityKey`, and `possibleDuplicate` descriptions/examples to match.\n\nThis satisfies the behavioural cases exercised by the tests: same lastName+postcode \u2192 same `householdId` (Cp11/Cp36); second such owner \u2192 409 unless `sharesHousehold` (Cp10/Cp35); declared member created and not flagged (Cp35); identity key uses the computed id and still collides on full duplicates (Cp03/Cp25/Cp28); household-size feeds membership level for shared households (Cp23).",
